      "namespace": "Nexudus.Authentication",
      "docPathPrefix": "rest-api/authentication",
      "status": "done",
      "notes": "No CRUD entities in this group - it is the auth mechanism, not record types. Fully covered by core NexudusClient: OAuth Bearer via password grant (+TOTP/2FA), refresh-token grant with automatic fallback to password on failure, static pre-acquired tokens, proactive refresh (expires_in + RefreshSkew), one-shot 401 retry, form-encoded token request to the 'token' endpoint. Documented Bearer + refresh flow is complete. Optional, NOT implemented (by design, non-entity, maintainer decision): (1) Basic Auth (appKey:secret / username:password Base64) for published-app/marketplace use; (2) 'Get Authentication Token for User' impersonation helper (Public API).",
